<title>ESTONIA: EBRD TO LAUNCH BALTIC EQUITY FUND.</title>
<headline>EBRD TO LAUNCH BALTIC EQUITY FUND.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development said on Monday it plans to launch an equity fund with $5 million for investments into small companies in Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania.</p>
<p>The fund, which will be registered off-shore and will operate in the Baltics under local management, still needs final approval, due to be discussed on August 27, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The fund will invest in small and medium-sized companies with turnover between $150,000 and $2 million. Investments will be in the range of $25,000 to $400,000.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
